## {{.Name}} — .forge-conventions

> Machine-readable convention file consumed by `forge lint`.
> Generated by forge new next-app (forge {{.ForgeVer}}).

convention: no-secrets-in-source
rule: Secrets, tokens, and credentials must never appear in source code — use environment variables.
severity: error
tags: security

convention: no-any
rule: Avoid TypeScript `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow explicitly.
severity: warning
tags: correctness dx

convention: no-silent-errors
rule: Errors must never be silently discarded. Catch blocks must log or rethrow.
severity: error
tags: correctness reliability

convention: server-components-default
rule: Next.js App Router components are Server Components by default. Only add 'use client' when required.
severity: warning
tags: performance nextjs

convention: no-client-env-secrets
rule: NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars are exposed to the browser. Never use them for secrets.
severity: error
tags: security nextjs

convention: health-endpoint-required
rule: App must expose /api/health returning {status:'ok'} for readiness probes.
severity: error
tags: reliability ops
